        ],
        [
          "öğretmen",
          "teacher"
        ]
      ],
      "quiz": [
        {
          "q": "How do you say « I am a student »?",
          "options": [
            "Öğrenciyim",
            "Öğrencisin",
            "Öğrenciyiz"
          ],
          "a": 0,
          "why": "With ben, you add -yim: öğrenci + yim = öğrenciyim."
        },
        {
          "q": "Which question means « How are you? » (formal you)?",
          "options": [
            "Nasılsın?",
            "Nasılsınız?",
            "Nerelisiniz?"
          ],
          "a": 1,
          "why": "The formal you adds -ınız: nasıl + sınız = nasılsınız."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "va1-3",
      "level": "A1",
      "num": 3,
      "title": "Plural, pronouns and demonstratives",
      "tr": "Çoğul, zamirler ve işaret sıfatları",
      "goal": "Say « the », point to a nearby or distant object and replace a noun with a pronoun.",
      "watch": "çoğul zamirler işaret",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The plural is formed with <b>-ler</b> or <b>-lar</b>, depending on the last vowel of the word: <tur>kitap → kitaplar</tur>, <tur>ev → evler</tur>, <tur>öğrenci → öğrenciler</tur>. After a number, the noun stays singular: <tur>üç kitap</tur> (three books)."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The personal pronouns",
          "head": [
            "Person",
            "Pronoun",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1st sing.",
              "<tur>ben</tur>",
              "me, I"
            ],
            [
              "2nd sing.",
              "<tur>sen</tur>",
              "you (informal)"
            ],
            [
              "3rd sing.",
              "<tur>o</tur>",
              "him, her"
            ],
            [
              "1st plur.",
              "<tur>biz</tur>",
              "we"
            ],
            [
              "2nd plur.",
              "<tur>siz</tur>",
              "you"
            ],
            [
              "3rd plur.",
              "<tur>onlar</tur>",
              "them"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The demonstratives",
          "head": [
            "Singular",
            "Plural",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<tur>bu</tur>",
              "<tur>bunlar</tur>",
              "this / these (near)"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>şu</tur>",
              "<tur>şunlar</tur>",
              "that / those (a little further away)"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>o</tur>",
              "<tur>onlar</tur>",
              "that / those (far away)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The demonstrative goes before the noun: <tur>bu kitap</tur> (this book), <tur>şu çanta</tur> (that bag), <tur>o araba</tur> (that car over there). In the plural: <tur>bu kitaplar</tur>, <tur>şu çantalar</tur>, <tur>o arabalar</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Bu kitaplar yeni.",
              "fr": "These books are new."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Şu çanta benim.",
              "fr": "That bag is mine."
            },
            {
              "tr": "O öğrenciler nereden geliyor?",
              "fr": "Where do those students come from?"
            },
            {
              "tr": "Her gün Türkçe çalışıyorum.",
              "fr": "I study Turkish every day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "The double o",
          "text": "<tur>O</tur> serves both as a pronoun (« he / she ») and as a distant demonstrative (« that … over there »). Context decides: <tur>O öğretmen</tur> = « that teacher over there »; <tur>O öğretmen.</tur> = « He is a teacher. »"
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        [
