      ],
      "quiz": [
        {
          "q": "Which question means « Where do you live? »?",
          "options": [
            "Nereye gidiyorsun?",
            "Nerede oturuyorsun?",
            "Nereden geliyorsun?"
          ],
          "a": 1,
          "why": "Nerede indicates the place where you are; oturuyorsun comes from oturmak (to live, to sit)."
        },
        {
          "q": "How do you ask « Are you a student? »?",
          "options": [
            "Öğrenci mi?",
            "Öğrenci misin?",
            "Öğrenci ne?"
          ],
          "a": 1,
          "why": "With sen, you add -sin and then the particle mi: öğrenci misin?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "va1-5",
      "level": "A1",
      "num": 5,
      "title": "Placing things: the cases of place",
      "tr": "Bulunma, yönelme ve ayrılma",
      "goal": "Say where you are, where you are going and where you come from with -de, -e and -den.",
      "watch": "bulunma yönelme ayrılma hali",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Three suffixes are enough to place an action. The <b>locative</b> <tur>-da / -de</tur> shows where you are. The <b>dative</b> <tur>-a / -e</tur> shows the destination. The <b>ablative</b> <tur>-dan / -den</tur> shows the origin."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The three cases of place",
          "head": [
            "Case",
            "Suffix",
            "ev (house)",
            "okul (school)",
            "sokak (street)"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Locative",
              "<tur>-da / -de</tur>",
              "<tur>evde</tur>",
              "<tur>okulda</tur>",
              "<tur>sokakta</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "Dative",
              "<tur>-a / -e</tur>",
              "<tur>eve</tur>",
              "<tur>okula</tur>",
              "<tur>sokağa</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "Ablative",
              "<tur>-dan / -den</tur>",
              "<tur>evden</tur>",
              "<tur>okuldan</tur>",
              "<tur>sokaktan</tur>"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "Voiceless consonants",
          "text": "After <b>p, ç, t, k, s, ş, f, h</b>, the d becomes t: <tur>kitapta</tur>, <tur>sokakta</tur>, <tur>açtan</tur>. After a vowel, the dative adds a linking y: <tur>masa → masaya</tur>, <tur>araba → arabaya</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "With the locative, <tur>var</tur> means « there is » and <tur>yok</tur> « there is not »: <tur>Evde su var.</tur> (There is water at home.) <tur>Okulda kimse yok.</tur> (There is nobody at school.)"
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Paris'te yaşıyorum.",
              "fr": "I live in Paris."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Okula gidiyorum.",
              "fr": "I am going to school."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Marketten geliyorum.",
              "fr": "I am coming back from the market."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Kitap masada.",
              "fr": "The book is on the table."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
