      ],
      "quiz": [
        {
          "q": "Which form means « to school » (destination)?",
          "options": [
            "okulda",
            "okula",
            "okuldan"
          ],
          "a": 1,
          "why": "The destination uses the dative -a: okul + a = okula."
        },
        {
          "q": "How do you say « from the house »?",
          "options": [
            "evde",
            "eve",
            "evden"
          ],
          "a": 2,
          "why": "The ablative -den shows the origin: ev + den = evden."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "va1-6",
      "level": "A1",
      "num": 6,
      "title": "Ordinal numbers and dates",
      "tr": "Sıra sayıları ve tarihler",
      "goal": "Say first, second, third…, ask for the date and talk about your birthday.",
      "watch": "sıra sayıları",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "To form an ordinal number, add <b>-inci / -ıncı / -üncü / -uncu</b> depending on the last vowel. The suffix agrees with the number: <tur>bir → birinci</tur>, <tur>iki → ikinci</tur>, <tur>üç → üçüncü</tur>, <tur>beş → beşinci</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The first ten ordinals",
          "head": [
            "Number",
            "Ordinal",
            "English"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<tur>bir</tur>",
              "<tur>birinci</tur>",
              "first"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>iki</tur>",
              "<tur>ikinci</tur>",
              "second"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>üç</tur>",
              "<tur>üçüncü</tur>",
              "third"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>dört</tur>",
              "<tur>dördüncü</tur>",
              "fourth"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>beş</tur>",
              "<tur>beşinci</tur>",
              "fifth"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>altı</tur>",
              "<tur>altıncı</tur>",
              "sixth"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>yedi</tur>",
              "<tur>yedinci</tur>",
              "seventh"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>sekiz</tur>",
              "<tur>sekizinci</tur>",
              "eighth"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>dokuz</tur>",
              "<tur>dokuzuncu</tur>",
              "ninth"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>on</tur>",
              "<tur>onuncu</tur>",
              "tenth"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "Watch out for dört",
          "text": "The final t of <tur>dört</tur> becomes <b>d</b> before a vowel: <tur>dördüncü</tur>. The same alternation appears in <tur>gitmek → gidiyorum</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "For the date, you say the month after the number: <tur>5 Mayıs</tur> (5 May). « What day of the month is it? » is <tur>Ayın kaçında?</tur> and the answer is <tur>Ayın beşinde.</tur> (on the fifth). For a birthday: <tur>Doğum günün ne zaman?</tur> — <tur>12 Mart'ta.</tur>"
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "İlk ders bugün.",
              "fr": "The first lesson is today."
            },
            {
              "tr": "İkinci katta oturuyorum.",
              "fr": "I live on the second floor."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Doğum günün ne zaman? — 12 Mart'ta.",
              "fr": "When is your birthday? — 12 March."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Sınav ayın kaçında?",
              "fr": "What day of the month is the test?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "Useful vocabulary",
          "text": "<tur>ilk</tur> = first (in a series), <tur>son</tur> = last, <tur>sonuncu</tur> = the last one (ordinal), <tur>kaçıncı</tur> = which number in the order. <tur>İlk kez</tur> means « for the first time »."
        }
      ],
