    {
      "id": "va1-8",
      "level": "A1",
      "num": 8,
      "title": "From… to…: -dan -e kadar",
      "tr": "-dan -e kadar",
      "goal": "Express a route, a duration or a limit with « from… to… / until ».",
      "watch": "-dan -e kadar",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The structure <b>-dan / -den … -a / -e kadar</b> means « from … to … » or « until … ». The first noun takes the ablative, the second the dative, and <tur>kadar</tur> closes the group: <tur>evden okula kadar</tur> (from home to school)."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "Three uses of kadar",
          "head": [
            "Structure",
            "Example",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Place",
              "<tur>Karaköyden Taksime kadar yürüdüm.</tur>",
              "I walked from Karaköy to Taksim."
            ],
            [
              "Time",
              "<tur>Dokuzdan beşe kadar çalışıyorum.</tur>",
              "I work from nine to five."
            ],
            [
              "Limit",
              "<tur>Akşama kadar bekledim.</tur>",
              "I waited until the evening."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "Vowel harmony and consonants",
          "text": "The suffixes follow the last vowel: <tur>evden eve kadar</tur>, <tur>okuldan okula kadar</tur>. After a voiceless consonant, <b>d</b> becomes <b>t</b>: <tur>sabahtan akşama kadar</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "You can also express distance: <tur>Evden okula kadar kaç kilometre?</tur> (How many kilometres is it from home to school?). And a time limit: <tur>Yarına kadar vaktim var.</tur> (I have time until tomorrow.)"
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Evden okula kadar yürüyorum.",
              "fr": "I walk from home to school."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Sabah dokuzdan akşam beşe kadar çalışıyorum.",
              "fr": "I work from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Taksime kadar metroyla gidiyorum.",
              "fr": "I go as far as Taksim by metro."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Yarına kadar bekleyelim.",
              "fr": "Let us wait until tomorrow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "Also « as much as »",
          "text": "<tur>Kadar</tur> can mean « as much as »: <tur>Senin kadar çalışıyorum.</tur> (I work as much as you.) The context shows whether it is a limit or a comparison."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        [
