    {
      "id": "va1-9",
      "level": "A1",
      "num": 9,
      "title": "Possession and var / yok",
      "tr": "İyelik ve var / yok",
      "goal": "Say what belongs to me, to you, to him, and express « there is » or « I do not have ».",
      "watch": "iyelik var yok",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Possession is marked by a suffix attached to the noun: <tur>evim</tur> (my house), <tur>evin</tur> (your house), <tur>evi</tur> (his / her house). You can reinforce it with the pronoun in the genitive: <tur>benim evim</tur>, <tur>senin evin</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "Possessive suffixes with ev (house)",
          "head": [
            "Person",
            "Form",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "benim",
              "<tur>evim</tur>",
              "my house"
            ],
            [
              "senin",
              "<tur>evin</tur>",
              "your house"
            ],
            [
              "onun",
              "<tur>evi</tur>",
              "his / her house"
            ],
            [
              "bizim",
              "<tur>evimiz</tur>",
              "our house"
            ],
            [
              "sizin",
              "<tur>eviniz</tur>",
              "your house"
            ],
            [
              "onların",
              "<tur>evleri</tur>",
              "their house"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "The linking s",
          "text": "After a vowel, the third person adds an <b>s</b>: <tur>araba → arabası</tur> (his / her car), <tur>çanta → çantası</tur>. After a consonant, the suffix is simply <tur>-i / -ı / -u / -ü</tur>: <tur>kitap → kitabı</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "<tur>Var</tur> means « there is / I have », <tur>yok</tur> « there is not / I do not have ». With a possessive, it becomes « to have »: <tur>Bir kardeşim var.</tur> (I have a brother.) <tur>Param yok.</tur> (I do not have any money.)"
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Benim adım Ali.",
              "fr": "My name is Ali."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Onun iki kardeşi var.",
              "fr": "He has two siblings."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Bizim evimiz küçük.",
              "fr": "Our house is small."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Sizin arabanız var mı?",
              "fr": "Do you have a car?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "Noun compounds",
          "text": "In a noun compound, the first noun stays bare and the second takes the third-person possessive: <tur>okul çantası</tur> (schoolbag, literally « the bag of the school »), <tur>Türkçe kitabı</tur> (Turkish book), <tur>mutfak masası</tur> (kitchen table)."
        }
      ],
